<div>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="mb-12">
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm mb-4">
            <a href="/docs/builtins" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Built-ins</a>
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-gray-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-white">Spreadsheet</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl mb-6">
            <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 to-cyan-400 bg-clip-text text-transparent">Spreadsheet Class</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-8">
            Import and parse CSV and Excel files for data processing.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CSV Functions -->
    <section id="section-csv" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">CSV Parsing</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-csv" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-csv" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.csv(content)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Parses a CSV string and returns an array of hashes (one hash per row).</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">csv_content = "name,email,age\nAlice,alice@example.com,30"
data = Spreadsheet.csv(csv_content)
print(data[0]["name"])  # "Alice"</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-csv-file" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-csv-file" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.csv_file(path)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Reads and parses a CSV file from disk.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">data = Spreadsheet.csv_file("users.csv")
for row in data
  print(row["email"])
end</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Excel Functions -->
    <section id="section-excel" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Excel Parsing</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-excel" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-excel" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.excel(path, sheet?)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Reads and parses one sheet of an Excel (.xlsx) file &mdash; the first, or the one named by <code class="text-amber-400">sheet</code>. Returns an array of hashes using the sheet&rsquo;s first row as headers. A sheet name the workbook does not have raises, listing the sheets it does have.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">data = Spreadsheet.excel("report.xlsx")
for row in data
  print(row["Name"])
end

orders = Spreadsheet.excel("report.xlsx", "Commandes")</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-excel-sheets" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-excel-sheets" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.excel_sheets(path)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Reads every sheet of an Excel (.xlsx) file. Returns a hash of sheet name &rArr; array of hashes, in the workbook&rsquo;s tab order &mdash; the same shape <code class="text-amber-400">excel_write</code> takes, so a workbook round-trips.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">sheets = Spreadsheet.excel_sheets("report.xlsx")
sheets.keys                 # ["Clients", "Commandes"]
sheets["Commandes"].length</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Export Functions -->
    <section id="section-export" class="scroll-mt-20 mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Export Functions</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6">
            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-to-csv" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-to-csv" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.to_csv(data)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Converts an array of hashes to a CSV string.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">data = [{"name": "Alice", "age": "30"}, {"name": "Bob", "age": "25"}]
csv = Spreadsheet.to_csv(data)</code></pre>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-3">Cells are written as CSV fields: one holding a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted (it used to shift columns or forge a row), and one that starts as a formula (<code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code>) gets a leading apostrophe so a spreadsheet opens it as text. Plain numbers are left as they are.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-csv-write" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-csv-write" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.csv_write(data, path)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Writes an array of hashes to a CSV file.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">data = [{"name": "Alice", "score": "95"}, {"name": "Bob", "score": "87"}]
Spreadsheet.csv_write(data, "output.csv")</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="fn-spreadsheet-excel-write" class="scroll-mt-20">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 p-5">
                    <a href="#fn-spreadsheet-excel-write" class="group flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <code class="text-lg font-mono text-amber-400">Spreadsheet.excel_write(data, path, columns?)</code>
                        <svg class="w-4 h-4 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 text-gray-500 transition-opacity" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1" />
                        </svg>
                    </a>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-3">Writes an array of hashes to an Excel (.xlsx) file, as one sheet named <code class="text-amber-400">Sheet1</code>. Without <code class="text-amber-400">columns</code>, the columns are the first row&rsquo;s keys in alphabetical order; with it, exactly those keys, in that order, as the header row (a key missing from a row leaves its cell empty). <code class="text-amber-400">Int</code> and <code class="text-amber-400">Float</code> values are written as numbers, so Excel can sum them; everything else is text, Strings included &mdash; a postcode or an order number keeps its leading zeros.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Example"><code class="language-soli text-sm">data = [{"name": "Alice", "score": 95}, {"name": "Bob", "score": 87}]
Spreadsheet.excel_write(data, "output.xlsx")

# Column order and headers of your choice
rows = orders.map { |o| {"Date": o.date, "N°": o.number, "Montant (€)": o.cents / 100.0} }
Spreadsheet.excel_write(rows, "tmp/orders.xlsx", ["Date", "N°", "Montant (€)"])</code></pre>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-3 mb-3"><strong class="text-white">Several sheets.</strong> Pass a hash instead of an array: each entry is one sheet, named by its key, in the hash&rsquo;s order. The value is the sheet&rsquo;s rows, or <code class="text-amber-400">{"rows": rows, "columns": [&hellip;]}</code> to choose its columns (with a hash, there is no third argument). Sheet names must be what Excel accepts &mdash; 1 to 31 characters, none of <code class="text-amber-400">: \ / ? * [ ]</code>, no leading or trailing apostrophe, not <code class="text-amber-400">History</code>, and unique ignoring case &mdash; or the call raises before writing anything.</p>
                    <pre data-filename="Several sheets"><code class="language-soli text-sm">Spreadsheet.excel_write({
  "Clients": clients.map { |c| {"Nom": c.name, "Ville": c.city} },
  "Commandes": {"rows": order_rows, "columns": ["Date", "N°", "Montant (€)"]}
}, "tmp/export.xlsx")</code></pre>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 mt-3 text-sm">To send it as a download, read it back as base64 &mdash; <code class="text-amber-400">uploaded_file_at(path)["data"]</code> &mdash; and return <code class="text-amber-400">{"status": 200, "headers": {"Content-Type": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet", "Content-Disposition": "attachment; filename=\"orders.xlsx\""}, "body_base64": data}</code>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12" id="section-untrusted">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Paths and Untrusted Workbooks</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Every path goes through the same jail as <code class="text-amber-400">File.*</code>: under <code class="text-amber-400">soli serve</code> (and in jobs) a relative path resolves under the app root, a path that escapes it raises <code class="text-amber-400">&hellip; escapes the app-root jail</code>, and a symlink is not followed &mdash; for <code class="text-amber-400">csv_file</code>, <code class="text-amber-400">excel</code> and <code class="text-amber-400">excel_sheets</code> as for <code class="text-amber-400">csv_write</code> and <code class="text-amber-400">excel_write</code>, which cannot truncate a file outside the app. <code class="text-amber-400">soli run</code>, the REPL and the test runner install no jail, as for <code class="text-amber-400">File</code>.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">A workbook a user uploaded is untrusted input. Before parsing one, <code class="text-amber-400">excel</code> and <code class="text-amber-400">excel_sheets</code> refuse a file over <code class="text-amber-400">SOLI_SPREADSHEET_MAX_BYTES</code> (default 50&nbsp;MiB) and one whose parts declare more than <code class="text-amber-400">SOLI_SPREADSHEET_MAX_INFLATED_BYTES</code> once inflated (default 512&nbsp;MiB); a file the parser cannot read &mdash; or panics on &mdash; raises an error of that call. The reader is calamine 0.38, which fixes RUSTSEC-2026-0436 (a panic and an unbounded allocation in the OLE2 parser every <code class="text-amber-400">.xlsx</code> goes through). These caps bound memory, not time: import large uploads in a background job rather than in the request.</p>
    </section>

</div>